\section*{Implementation Outcomes (Phase 4--5)}

This report was written in November 2025 during Phase~1. The following documents which pivot recommendations were adopted, which were modified, and which were not taken.

\subsection*{Pivot A: Kusama + Polkadot Dual Deployment}

\textbf{Status: Not adopted.} The implementation used a local Zombienet testnet (Rococo-local) rather than deploying to Kusama or Polkadot. This was sufficient for thesis evaluation. Deployment to Kusama/Polkadot is documented as future work.

\subsection*{Pivot B: RMRK 2.0 + Scheduled XCM}

\textbf{Status: Not adopted as recommended. Significant pivot required.}

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{Pivot B: Recommendation vs Outcome}
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{LLL}
\toprule
\textbf{Recommendation} & \textbf{What Happened} & \textbf{Why} \\
\midrule
Use RMRK 2.0 as rights token & Used \texttt{pallet-nfts} instead & RMRK 2.0 pallets were abandoned by the community---frozen at polkadot-v0.9.36, incompatible with current polkadot-sdk. \\
Scheduled XCM for auto-renewal & Used \texttt{on\_initialize} hook pattern & XCM v5 \texttt{Schedule} instruction is not production-ready. The on-chain scheduler achieves the same result. \\
``First production use of scheduled XCM + RMRK'' & Contribution reframed & Thesis contribution is: first unified cross-chain content rights pallet with subscription + PPV + ownership + automatic royalty propagation + Ethereum bridge via Snowbridge. \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
\end{table}

The core thesis contribution remains valid---the system is the first known implementation combining all three monetisation models in a single cross-chain rights primitive.

\subsection*{Pivot C: On-Demand Coretime via Asset Hub}

\textbf{Status: Not applicable.} Local Zombienet testnet was used instead of any coretime model. On-demand coretime remains a viable deployment option for future production use.

